oeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Review-defect correction implemented at f019a187d4de4335ba003b734666f293ccb8be25, preserving Change-Id Ie76ef5d4d4d4b2a4beec3b946822c6622161c8b6. The allowlisted S3 shim comment now states why the adjacent runtime stderr is exact and shrinks 10 -> 7 words; the runtime string is byte-identical.\n\nPost-amend evidence: immutable-prose-only PASS for all 13 paths; exact-leaf-paths PASS; comment-hygiene PASS; focused consumers 12/12 PASS; diff-integrity PASS; pre-commit Ruff and full mypy PASS; verify-commit-ticket PASS. Per the comments-only waiver, make verify remains intentionally omitted and Gerrit CI will supply the full gate. Because the coordinator authored this correction after finding it, a different agent must perform the fresh 52-row non-author semantic review before push.","timestamp":1788876097208493001}],"created_at":1788571030445200204,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"cef8bb65-d066-4996-8f9b-8ba384468a6d","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"0e15-a2f2-76e1-4ccd"},{"link_uuid":"3d8df97c-c237-4e29-a860-d18de75f31b3","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"9479-0ec6-bb65-428d"},{"link_uuid":"e147fdaa-c417-426c-9a71-ab5bdff11ee2","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"f11d-61b5-b06c-4c53"},{"link_uuid":"5efc060e-b6fd-445f-9dfc-2933058bbbc1","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"78cd-62d1-8c80-42de"},{"link_uuid":"a5083a53-e154-4443-bdba-982c87ea73d7","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"cd29-ba08-4fa5-442a"},{"link_uuid":"04c3db8f-4884-40eb-a282-f811bfb0ed8b","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"1a6a-405a-1bb0-4ae9"},{"link_uuid":"92bf55be-9b6b-4252-ad38-acb105b7334f","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"0d84-efab-9822-4afc"},{"link_uuid":"712e2e20-d520-4cf6-ad31-57bfa00aabda","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"3694-596c-7e64-4bce"},{"link_uuid":"2eaa0c45-e357-4838-902f-87d1d3b501ee","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"e860-2191-8a29-4e8e"},{"link_uuid":"5213da19-44b6-43a7-99dd-3ffa7e0a0710","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"4ba4-a5dc-1e9d-4b3a"},{"link_uuid":"0964f1b9-adb6-4c08-a5d8-ab8010d3b778","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"ea64-4472-fbc4-4142"},{"link_uuid":"7f2a8971-5622-4b0f-9546-302760be33cc","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"e12b-91c9-24ac-4782"}],"description":"## Context / immutable audit base\nAt `origin/main@88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684`, 13 integration-test files contain exactly 52 editable blocks: 35 true leading docstrings and 17 full-line comment regions, 6,045 before-words. The prior 51-block plan is preserved and rebased; `test_epoch_guard_reconciliation.py#D:_clone_tickets` is the sole delta addition. Bracketed counts use `(?u)\\b[^\\W_]\\w*(?:[-'][^\\W_]\\w*)*\\b`.\n\n## Exact prose allowlist\n`D:<owner>` is a leading owner docstring; `C:<owner>:before:<anchor>` is one maximal full-line comment region. `@start-end[count]` gives the immutable span and word count.\n\n- `s3_doctor_harness.py` — `D:<module>@1-21[149]`.\n- `test_b636_rebuild_history_loss.py` — `D:<module>@1-12[97]`, `D:test_restore_falls_back_to_per_uuid_lookup@279-282[51]`.\n- `test_bare_repository_fixture_portability_heldout.py` — `D:<module>@1-71[668]`, `C:<module>:before:EXCLUDED_FILES@94-98[49]`.\n- `test_concurrency_regression.py` — `D:<module>@1-19[145]`, `D:_make_repo@79-90[117]`, `D:_expire_sync_marker@102-112[96]`, `D:_sync_from_origin@121-142[201]`, `D:_reconverge_by_read_sync@148-164[159]`, `D:test_fixture_remote_runs_no_detached_upkeep_and_shares_no_objects@324-330[64]`, `C:test_two_clone_union_deterministic_replay_and_fork_tiebreak:before:listing@422-426[58]`, `C:test_two_clone_union_deterministic_replay_and_fork_tiebreak:before:seed_status_events@442-456[147]`, `C:test_two_clone_set_tags_table_converges:before:_engine_run@549-551[39]`, `C:<module>:before:_FAST_NOW@587-591[46]`, `C:<module>:before:_DRAKE_PUSH_CODE@804-813[99]`, `D:test_sub_horizon_append_orphan_recovered_by_fsck_rebuild@1054-1061[66]`, `D:test_a3_marker_is_optimization_not_authority_crash_before_marker@1325-1328[51]`, `D:test_two_clone_compaction_resurrection_no_data_loss_and_repairable@1374-1380[67]`, `C:test_rebuild_restarts_from_stale_bak_sentinel:before:create_file@1420-1425[68]`, `D:_tickets_merge_count@1492-1501[91]`, `D:test_cas_backoff_refetch_lands_all_writes_under_real_contention@1506-1517[115]`, `C:<module>:before:_engine_run_env@1619-1634[174]`, `D:test_scenario_a_normal_horizon_real_remote_append_visible_no_repair@1665-1676[131]`, `C:test_scenario_a_normal_horizon_real_remote_append_visible_no_repair:before:_sync_from_origin@1721-1724[50]`, `D:test_scenario_b_far_future_snapshot_orphan_real_fsck_repair_converges@1755-1767[121]`, `C:test_scenario_b_far_future_snapshot_orphan_real_fsck_repair_converges:before:state_a@1851-1855[53]`, `C:<module>:before:_last_id@1876-1880[51]`, `D:test_parent_cascade_same_tracker_race_winner_takes_parent_loser_aborts@1904-1924[205]`, `D:_assert_emit_is_append_only@2190-2198[90]`.\n- `test_ensure_project_mapping.py` — `D:<module>@1-17[133]`.\n- `test_id_collision.py` — `D:<module>@1-19[169]`.\n- `test_prepare_reclaim_backup.py` — `D:test_backup_fixture_remote_leaves_no_detached_upkeep@639-656[174]`.\n- `test_reconcile_live_e2e.py` — `D:<module>@1-42[331]`, `C:<module>:before:pytestmark@59-67[106]`, `C:<module>:before:RECON_DIR sys.path guard@78-80[36]`, `C:<module>:before:_MOD_CACHE@84-92[107]`, `C:<module>:before:@_requires_live@328-334[45]`, `D:_fresh_search@394-412[175]`, `D:_poll_until_visible@462-476[138]`, `D:test_poll_until_visible_waits_out_slow_index_convergence@523-529[62]`, `D:_IndexLaggingAcliRun@571-577[58]`, `D:test_poll_until_visible_requeries_a_real_client_until_the_index_converges@595-606[117]`.\n- `test_s3_doctor_heldout.py` — `D:<module>@1-21[165]`.\n- `test_s3_doctor.py` — `D:<module>@1-15[107]`, `C:_install_git_shim:before:bad-object stderr@62[10]`, `D:test_heal_rides_out_a_transient_bad_object_from_the_bundle_step@131-139[96]`, `C:<module>:before:_bundle_contains@203-209[83]`.\n- `test_s3_preflight.py` — `D:<module>@1-14[135]`.\n- `test_store_concurrency.py` — `D:<module>@1-19[182]`, `D:test_concurrent_writer_storm_no_loss@131-135[57]`.\n- `test_epoch_guard_reconciliation.py` — `D:_clone_tickets@52-58[41]`.\n\n## Contracts, consumers, and protected prose\nRetain real-Git union/fork/CAS/recovery behavior, pinned bare-repository portability, live-Jira confinement, polling/backoff, S3 lossless healing, and parent-cascade/append-only evidence. The new clone docstring must still explain why stderr is surfaced without changing the runtime error strings. Consumers are pytest, integration/held-out suites, reusable harness imports, the live-Jira guard, and comment hygiene.\n\nAll unlisted prose is protected, including the epoch module's concise module docstring, executable subprocess/error strings, assertions, runtime fixture programs, and all statement-attached directives.\n\n## Preservation and review contract\nCompare immutable `88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:<path>` blobs with the final commit. Parse Python with `ast.parse(..., type_comments=True)`; remove only the allowlisted leading owner docstrings; normalize only `ast.TypeIgnore.lineno`; require the remaining AST to match. Reject changes to inline or non-allowlisted comments. Preserve runtime strings, assertions, decorators, test data, shebangs, and every directive-bearing physical line exactly. Only adjacent blank-line normalization is allowed.\n\nA reviewer who did not author the leaf must post exactly 52 leaf-linked TSV rows:\n`stable_block_id<TAB>before_citation<TAB>final_citation<TAB>preserved_contract_or_consumer<TAB>directives_exact<TAB>before_words<TAB>after_words<TAB>semantic-preservation<TAB>bloat-removal<TAB>reviewer_session`.\nBefore citations use `88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:<path>#<stable-id>`; final citations use `<full-final-sha>:<path>#<stable-id>`. Every row must have `after_words < before_words` and all three verdict fields PASS.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The one-commit changed-path set is exactly the 13-path file-impact set.\n- [ ] Only the 52 declared prose blocks and adjacent blank lines change.\n- [ ] The normalized non-docstring AST is identical on every impacted path.\n- [ ] Runtime strings and non-allowlisted comments remain byte-identical.\n- [ ] Directive and shebang physical lines remain byte-identical and attached.\n- [ ] The independent TSV has exactly 52 passing rows.\n- [ ] Every recorded DD command passes, including the no-timeout worktree-venv `make verify`.\n","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/integration/s3_doctor_harness.py","reason":"Condense the real-bundle S3 harness contract."},{"path":"tests/integration/test_b636_rebuild_history_loss.py","reason":"Condense snapshot-loss recovery and per-UUID fallback prose."},{"path":"tests/integration/test_bare_repository_fixture_portability_heldout.py","reason":"Condense bare-repository portability sweep prose."},{"path":"tests/integration/test_concurrency_regression.py","reason":"Condense real-Git convergence, recovery, cascade, and append-only prose."},{"path":"tests/integration/test_ensure_project_mapping.py","reason":"Condense project-mapping seed/stamp contract prose."},{"path":"tests/integration/test_epoch_guard_reconciliation.py","reason":"Condense clone-failure diagnosis prose while preserving stderr behavior."},{"path":"tests/integration/test_id_collision.py","reason":"Condense canonical-ID and deterministic-alias collision prose."},{"path":"tests/integration/test_prepare_reclaim_backup.py","reason":"Condense pinned-backup-remote evidence prose."},{"path":"tests/integration/test_reconcile_live_e2e.py","reason":"Condense live-Jira confinement, polling, and cache prose."},{"path":"tests/integration/test_s3_doctor_heldout.py","reason":"Condense held-out S3 safety and conflict prose."},{"path":"tests/integration/test_s3_doctor.py","reason":"Condense lossless healing and transient-retry prose."},{"path":"tests/integration/test_s3_preflight.py","reason":"Condense fail-closed S3 preflight prose."},{"path":"tests/integration/test_store_concurrency.py","reason":"Condense permanent locking and writer-survival prose."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","2d43-3c39-307e-4450"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"2d43-3c39-307e-4450","parent_status_uuid":"9d5078ea-c429-48b5-b4ba-8965bb14290a","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":["rebar"],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["comments","documentation","maintainability","grouped-remediation"],"ticket_id":"46e0-1134-708b-4752","ticket_type":"task","title":"Condense comments in tests/integration","verify_commands":[{"command":"rtk env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python -c 'import ast, difflib, io, json, os, re, subprocess, tokenize\nBASE=\"88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684\"\nAFTER=os.environ.get(\"REBAR_AFTER_REF\",\"HEAD\")\nSPEC=json.loads(\"\"\"{\"tests/integration/s3_doctor_harness.py\":{\"docs\":[\"<module>\"],\"spans\":[[1,21]]},\"tests/integration/test_b636_rebuild_history_loss.py\":{\"docs\":[\"<module>\",\"test_restore_falls_back_to_per_uuid_lookup\"],\"spans\":[[1,12],[279,282]]},\"tests/integration/test_bare_repository_fixture_portability_heldout.py\":{\"docs\":[\"<module>\"],\"spans\":[[1,71],[94,98]]},\"tests/integration/test_concurrency_regression.py\":{\"docs\":[\"<module>\",\"_make_repo\",\"_expire_sync_marker\",\"_sync_from_origin\",\"_reconverge_by_read_sync\",\"test_fixture_remote_runs_no_detached_upkeep_and_shares_no_objects\",\"test_sub_horizon_append_orphan_recovered_by_fsck_rebuild\",\"test_a3_marker_is_optimization_not_authority_crash_before_marker\",\"test_two_clone_compaction_resurrection_no_data_loss_and_repairable\",\"_tickets_merge_count\",\"test_cas_backoff_refetch_lands_all_writes_under_real_contention\",\"test_scenario_a_normal_horizon_real_remote_append_visible_no_repair\",\"test_scenario_b_far_future_snapshot_orphan_real_fsck_repair_converges\",\"test_parent_cascade_same_tracker_race_winner_takes_parent_loser_aborts\",\"_assert_emit_is_append_only\"],\"spans\":[[1,19],[79,90],[102,112],[121,142],[148,164],[324,330],[422,426],[442,456],[549,551],[587,591],[804,813],[1054,1061],[1325,1328],[1374,1380],[1420,1425],[1492,1501],[1506,1517],[1619,1634],[1665,1676],[1721,1724],[1755,1767],[1851,1855],[1876,1880],[1904,1924],[2190,2198]]},\"tests/integration/test_ensure_project_mapping.py\":{\"docs\":[\"<module>\"],\"spans\":[[1,17]]},\"tests/integration/test_epoch_guard_reconciliation.py\":{\"docs\":[\"_clone_tickets\"],\"spans\":[[52,58]]},\"tests/integration/test_id_collision.py\":{\"docs\":[\"<module>\"],\"spans\":[[1,19]]},\"tests/integration/test_prepare_reclaim_backup.py\":{\"docs\":[\"test_backup_fixture_remote_leaves_no_detached_upkeep\"],\"spans\":[[639,656]]},\"tests/integration/test_reconcile_live_e2e.py\":{\"docs\":[\"<module>\",\"_fresh_search\",\"_poll_until_visible\",\"test_poll_until_visible_waits_out_slow_index_convergence\",\"_IndexLaggingAcliRun\",\"test_poll_until_visible_requeries_a_real_client_until_the_index_converges\"],\"spans\":[[1,42],[59,67],[78,80],[84,92],[328,334],[394,412],[462,476],[523,529],[571,577],[595,606]]},\"tests/integration/test_s3_doctor_heldout.py\":{\"docs\":[\"<module>\"],\"spans\":[[1,21]]},\"tests/integration/test_s3_doctor.py\":{\"docs\":[\"<module>\",\"test_heal_rides_out_a_transient_bad_object_from_the_bundle_step\"],\"spans\":[[1,15],[62,62],[131,139],[203,209]]},\"tests/integration/test_s3_preflight.py\":{\"docs\":[\"<module>\"],\"spans\":[[1,14]]},\"tests/integration/test_store_concurrency.py\":{\"docs\":[\"<module>\",\"test_concurrent_writer_storm_no_loss\"],\"spans\":[[1,19],[131,135]]}}\"\"\")\nOWNERS=(ast.Module,ast.ClassDef,ast.FunctionDef,ast.AsyncFunctionDef)\nPAT=re.compile(r\"#\\\\s*(?:noqa\\\\b|type:\\\\s*ignore\\\\b|pragma:\\\\s*no cover\\\\b|pyright:|mypy:|ruff:|pylint:|(?:fmt|isort):\\\\s*(?:on|off|skip)\\\\b|nosec\\\\b|coding[:=]|[A-Za-z][\\\\w-]*-ok:)\",re.I)\ndef src(ref,path):\n return subprocess.check_output([\"git\",\"show\",f\"{ref}:{path}\"],text=True)\ndef strip_docs(tree,allowed,required):\n seen=set()\n def visit(node,prefix):\n  if isinstance(node,ast.Module):\n   name=\"<module>\"; child_prefix=prefix\n  elif isinstance(node,(ast.ClassDef,ast.FunctionDef,ast.AsyncFunctionDef)):\n   name=\".\".join((*prefix,node.name)); child_prefix=(*prefix,node.name)\n  else:\n   for child in ast.iter_child_nodes(node): visit(child,prefix)\n   return\n  if name in allowed and node.body and isinstance(node.body[0],ast.Expr) and isinstance(node.body[0].value,ast.Constant) and isinstance(node.body[0].value.value,str):\n   node.body.pop(0); seen.add(name)\n  for child in ast.iter_child_nodes(node): visit(child,child_prefix)\n visit(tree,())\n if required: assert seen==set(allowed),f\"missing allowlisted docstrings: {sorted(set(allowed)-seen)}\"\n return tree\ndef norm(text,path,allowed,required):\n tree=strip_docs(ast.parse(text,filename=path,type_comments=True),allowed,required)\n for node in ast.walk(tree):\n  if isinstance(node,ast.TypeIgnore): node.lineno=0\n return ast.dump(tree,annotate_fields=True,include_attributes=False)\ndef directives(text):\n lines=text.splitlines()\n picked=[lines[t.start[0]-1] for t in tokenize.generate_tokens(io.StringIO(text).readline) if t.type==tokenize.COMMENT and PAT.search(t.string)]\n return (lines[0] if lines and lines[0].startswith(\"#!\") else \"\"),picked\ndef admitted(line,lines,spans):\n return any(s<=line<=e for s,e in spans) or (1<=line<=len(lines) and not lines[line-1].strip() and any(s-1<=line<=e+1 for s,e in spans))\nfor path,rule in SPEC.items():\n before=src(BASE,path); after=src(AFTER,path)\n assert norm(before,path,rule[\"docs\"],True)==norm(after,path,rule[\"docs\"],False),f\"runtime AST changed: {path}\"\n assert directives(before)==directives(after),f\"directive/shebang changed: {path}\"\n a=before.splitlines(); b=after.splitlines()\n for tag,i1,i2,j1,j2 in difflib.SequenceMatcher(a=a,b=b,autojunk=False).get_opcodes():\n  if tag==\"equal\": continue\n  if i1==i2:\n   assert any(s-1<=i1<=e for s,e in rule[\"spans\"]),f\"insertion outside allowlist: {path}:{i1+1}\"\n  else:\n   bad=[line for line in range(i1+1,i2+1) if not admitted(line,a,rule[\"spans\"])]\n   assert not bad,f\"changed base lines outside allowlist: {path}:{bad}\"\nprint(f\"immutable prose oracle PASS: {len(SPEC)} paths at {BASE} -> {AFTER}\")'","dd_id":"immutable-prose-only","dd_text":"Immutable-base AST, allowlisted-span, and directive/shebang oracle passes."},{"command":"rtk env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python -c 'import json, subprocess\nexpected=set(json.loads(\"\"\"[\"tests/integration/s3_doctor_harness.py\",\"tests/integration/test_b636_rebuild_history_loss.py\",\"tests/integration/test_bare_repository_fixture_portability_heldout.py\",\"tests/integration/test_concurrency_regression.py\",\"tests/integration/test_ensure_project_mapping.py\",\"tests/integration/test_epoch_guard_reconciliation.py\",\"tests/integration/test_id_collision.py\",\"tests/integration/test_prepare_reclaim_backup.py\",\"tests/integration/test_reconcile_live_e2e.py\",\"tests/integration/test_s3_doctor_heldout.py\",\"tests/integration/test_s3_doctor.py\",\"tests/integration/test_s3_preflight.py\",\"tests/integration/test_store_concurrency.py\"]\"\"\"))\nactual=set(subprocess.check_output([\"git\",\"diff\",\"--name-only\",\"HEAD^\",\"HEAD\"],text=True).splitlines())\nassert actual==expected,f\"changed paths differ: missing={sorted(expected-actual)} extra={sorted(actual-expected)}\"'","dd_id":"exact-leaf-paths","dd_text":"The one-commit changed-path set exactly equals file impact."},{"command":"rtk env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py","dd_id":"comment-hygiene","dd_text":"Repository comment-history hygiene passes."},{"command":"rtk env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/integration/test_epoch_guard_reconciliation.py tests/unit/test_comment_hygiene_guard.py::test_the_real_tree_is_clean tests/integration/test_bare_repository_fixture_portability_heldout.py::test_no_test_addresses_a_bare_repository_by_discovery tests/unit/test_live_jira_xdist_confinement.py::test_every_live_jira_test_is_xdist_group_confined tests/integration/test_s3_doctor.py::test_heal_collapses_two_bundles_losslessly tests/integration/test_reconcile_live_e2e.py::test_poll_until_visible_requeries_a_real_client_until_the_index_converges","dd_id":"focused-contracts","dd_text":"Focused direct consumers of the edited prose paths pass."},{"command":"rtk git diff --check HEAD^ HEAD -- tests/integration/s3_doctor_harness.py tests/integration/test_b636_rebuild_history_loss.py tests/integration/test_bare_repository_fixture_portability_heldout.py tests/integration/test_concurrency_regression.py tests/integration/test_ensure_project_mapping.py tests/integration/test_epoch_guard_reconciliation.py tests/integration/test_id_collision.py tests/integration/test_prepare_reclaim_backup.py tests/integration/test_reconcile_live_e2e.py tests/integration/test_s3_doctor_heldout.py tests/integration/test_s3_doctor.py tests/integration/test_s3_preflight.py tests/integration/test_store_concurrency.py","dd_id":"diff-integrity","dd_text":"Owned-path patch has no whitespace errors."},{"command":"rtk env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make verify","dd_id":"repository-gates","dd_text":"The complete locally checkable CI contract passes before push."}]},"source_event_uuids":["f6c8d2c3-6644-45ed-9524-7d7b081befda","a779abc8-b515-4b84-a443-bc805507aedc","e8667497-112a-4cea-a6f1-ac78e9ebde54","72e1773f-07d9-4650-842e-d11d20f67140","5671d551-08cf-41dc-a5e0-9ef2a3797edf","3bc3ac06-9d1f-49c3-a26f-75b7590e375d","344ed2d2-c462-4617-bb00-973e5f9910d7","9d5078ea-c429-48b5-b4ba-8965bb14290a","0ed0d661-af61-4981-bb31-661b24dc604f","f7a0e261-d5cc-4e57-ab03-aca9750fe360","02ccbe77-edad-4de8-b891-4c44b18e6068","145f69cf-c72e-4364-ae59-cd80e42ac125"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788884971508294001,"uuid":"c844735b-e705-4f21-b9ca-f17fad1aeaca"}